markdown <<MARKDOWN
## Localize test
The previous version had all the text buried inside a JavaScript object (const LANG = {...}). Localize works by scanning what's actually visible in the HTML page. If text only exists inside a JS variable, Localize either misses it entirely or needs extra configuration to find it. So the goal was to get every single word out of JavaScript and into the HTML.

The 4 specific things that were changed:
1. All user-facing text moved into HTML elements
Every button label, heading, instruction, feedback message, and character dialogue now lives in an actual HTML tag — a p, h2, span, div. Localize scans these automatically. Nothing your team needs to translate is hiding in JS.
2. Every translatable element got a data-i18n attribute
For example: <button data-i18n="btn-start">Comenzar a Depurar con Alex →</button>. The data-i18n value is a unique key like btn-start or check1-title. This isn't strictly required by Localize, but it gives the dashboard a clean reference name for each string, makes it easy to search the source file, and is good practice if the team ever wants to export translations as a JSON file.
3. Code syntax is protected with data-translate="no"
The actual for loop, console.log(i), variable names, and the filename are wrapped in data-translate="no". This is a standard attribute Localize respects — it tells the platform to skip those elements completely so the code never gets accidentally translated.
4. Dynamic text uses hidden HTML templates instead of JS strings
Some text gets generated at runtime — like "Verificación 3 de 6" — where the number changes. Instead of building that string in JavaScript ("Verificación " + n + " de 6"), there's now a hidden <span> in the HTML that holds the template text (Verificación {n} de 6). Localize can see and translate that template. Then JavaScript just reads the already-translated template text and swaps in the number. The JS never owns the words.


<div style="width:100%; max-width:900px; margin:0 auto; border-radius:16px; overflow:hidden; box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(124,58,237,0.2); border:1px solid #2d3350;">
  <iframe 
    src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/Unit4_testing/como_probar_codigo_loops_ia_localize.html"
    width="100%" 
    height="780" 
    frameborder="0">
  </iframe>
</div>










MARKDOWN
